 The Hive table schema is kept in sync with the Iceberg table. If an outside source (Impala/Spark/Java API/etc)
 changes the schema, the Hive table immediately reflects the changes. You alter the table schema using Hive commands:
 
+!!! warning
+    The Hive Metastore stores the Hive table schema separately from the Iceberg table metadata. If the Hive table
+    schema is changed directly in the Hive Metastore (for example, by a Hive version or tool that is not aware of
+    Iceberg), the two schemas can diverge. Subsequent Iceberg schema-evolution operations may then fail or produce
+    unexpected results because the Hive schema no longer matches the Iceberg schema. To avoid this, perform schema
+    changes through an Iceberg-aware engine (such as Hive 4.0.0 or later with Iceberg integration, Spark, or the
+    Iceberg Java API) so that both schemas are updated together.
+
 * Rename a table
 ```sql
 ALTER TABLE orders RENAME TO renamed_orders;
